2. Web4 Public Asset Definition

A Web4 Public Asset is a person, company, brand, token, dataset, AI agent, media property, or cultural artifact that is prepared for public participation through disclosure, consent, governance, and jurisdictional reporting.

A Web4 Public Asset may include:

1. A public-facing brand.
2. A tokenized economic layer.
3. A tokenized likeness or persona layer.
4. An AI-assisted media layer.
5. A governance and disclosure layer.
6. A GitHub-based documentation layer.
7. A jurisdiction-specific compliance dataset.
8. A revenue-sharing or licensing model.

